    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6674145">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183"/>
        <mathmoddb:P983 xml:lang="en">&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; class=&quot;mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle=&quot;true&quot; scriptlevel=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;A&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
        <mathmoddb:P983 xml:lang="en">&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; class=&quot;mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle=&quot;true&quot; scriptlevel=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;B&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
        <mathmoddb:P983 xml:lang="en">&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; class=&quot;mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle=&quot;true&quot; scriptlevel=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
        <mathmoddb:P983 xml:lang="en">&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; class=&quot;mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle=&quot;true&quot; scriptlevel=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;W&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;c&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
        <mathmoddb:P989 xml:lang="en">&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; class=&quot;mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle=&quot;true&quot; scriptlevel=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;A&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;W&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;c&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;+&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;W&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;c&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mi&gt;A&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot; lspace=&quot;0&quot; rspace=&quot;0&quot;&gt;∗&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;+&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;munder&gt;&lt;mo movablelimits=&quot;false&quot; stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;∑&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;k&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/munder&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;k&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;W&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;c&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;msubsup&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;k&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot; lspace=&quot;0&quot; rspace=&quot;0&quot;&gt;∗&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msubsup&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;+&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;B&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mi&gt;B&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot; lspace=&quot;0&quot; rspace=&quot;0&quot;&gt;∗&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;0&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P989>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Lyapunov generalized controllability</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">For a numerical solution, one can resort to iterative schemes, which requires the solution of a standard Lyapunov equation in each step. As an alternative, one may use the biconjugate gradient method (with preconditioner) as suggested by Tobias Breiten from TU Graz, Austria, now TU Berlin.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">For the solvability of generalized Lyapunov equations, there are two requirements: (1) stability condition for A and (2) suitable upper bound for the norm of N.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1684 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6674151"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyapunov_equation"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1028945"/>
        <mathmoddb:P558 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6482447"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">generalized Lyapunov equation used in the stability analysis of linear dynamical systems to determine the controllability</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
