        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Liouville equation</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P104 rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liouville%27s_equation"/>
        <mathmoddb:P12 xml:lang="en">Q20180666</mathmoddb:P12>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Consider a Hamiltonian dynamical system with canonical coordinates and conjugate momenta. Then the phase space distribution  determines the probability that the system will be found in the infinitesimal phase space volume.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Note the similarity with the quantum Liouville (von Neumann) equation where the  Poisson brackets {.,.} are replaced by commutator brackets [.,.]</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1674 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6674256"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liouville%27s_theorem_(Hamiltonian)"/>
        <mathmoddb:P558 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6482292"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">partial differential equation for the that time rate of change of density of points in phase space</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
