        <mathmoddb:P989 xml:lang="en">&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; class=&quot;mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle=&quot;true&quot; scriptlevel=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi mathvariant=&quot;normal&quot;&gt;R&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi mathvariant=&quot;normal&quot;&gt;e&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;≪&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;1&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P989>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">creeping flow assumption</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Volker John: If the viscous transport dominates the convective transport, i.e. if the fluid flows very slowly, the non-linear convective term of the Navier–Stokes equations can be neglected. This gives a linear equation, the so-called Stokes equations.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stokes_flow"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://www.wias-berlin.de/people/john/LEHRE/NUM_CFD/num_cfd_1.pdf"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q674202"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">fluid flow where advective inertial forces are small compared with viscous forces</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
