    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6675320 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6675320">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Maxwell&apos;s equations</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P104 rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maxwell%27s_equations"/>
        <mathmoddb:P12 xml:lang="en">Q51501</mathmoddb:P12>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Given the charge density ρ(r, t) and the current density j(r, t), Maxwell&apos;s equations yield the electric and magnetic fields, E(r, t) and B(r, t). These equations are the simplest representative of a more general class of models, also referred as Maxwell&apos;s equations, where ρ(r, t) and j(r, t) should be found from certain additional relations, e.g., from the Ohm&apos;s law.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Together with the Lorentz force law, Maxwell&apos;s equations form the foundation of classical electromagnetism and optics. The equations provide a mathematical model for electric, optical, and radio technologies.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270"/>
        <mathmoddb:P147 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6684565"/>
        <mathmoddb:P147 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6684609"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6674127"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6674353"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6674372"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6674373"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1674 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6674480"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1684 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6675438"/>
        <mathmoddb:P286 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6672241"/>
        <mathmoddb:P558 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6482471"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">set of four coupled partial differential equations describing how electric and magnetic fields are generated and altered by each other and by charges and currents</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



