    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775500 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775500">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">heavy particle propagation</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Note that in quantum-classical dynamics the forces acting on the heavy particles depend on the quantum state of the light particles.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">The classical trajectories can be integrated with conventional methods, as the Verlet algorithm. Such integration requires the forces acting on the nuclei. They are proportional to the gradient of the potential energy of the electronic states.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixed_quantum-classical_dynamics"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">propagating the (classical!) state of the heavy particle(s) in quantum-classical dynamics models</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775501 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775501">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">heavy particle velocity adjustment</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">If the classical kinetic energy can aﬀord the energy cost of the quantum transition, the nuclei switch simultaneously to the new PES. The nuclear positions are kept unchanged and the nuclear velocities are adjusted along the direction of the nonadiabatic (NA) coupling vector to conserve total energy. Otherwise, the surface hop is rejected. This procedure is essential to achieve Boltzmann quantum state populations and detailed balance between hops up and down in energy.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">adjusting heavy particle(s) velocity upon nonadiabatic transitions in quantum-classical dynamics</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775502 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775502">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">light particle nonadiabatic transitions</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Note that in quantum-classical dynamics the effective Hamiltonian governing the non-adiabatic transitions of the light particles parametrically depends on the heavy particle(s) positions.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Typically, the many different approaches to quantum-classical dynamics, most notably surface hopping trajectories, differ in the way how the nonadiabatic transition probabilities are calculated.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixed_quantum-classical_dynamics"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">nonadiabatic transitions of the light particle(s) in quantum-classical dynamics models</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775503 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775503">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">light particle propagation</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Note that in quantum-classical dynamics the effective Hamiltonian governing the quantum dynamics of the light particles parametrically depends on the heavy particle(s) positions.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">The electrons are usually treated by a local approximation of the TDSE, i.e., they depend only on the electronic forces and couplings at the instantaneous position of the nuclei.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775478"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixed_quantum-classical_dynamics"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1690 rdf:resource="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q65091550"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">propagating the (quantum!) state of the light particle(s) in quantum-classical dynamics models</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



