    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821277 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821277">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">computation of crop phenological development stage</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This task computes the physiological development stage of a crop based on accumulated thermal time. Using daily temperature inputs and crop-specific thermal thresholds, the task calculates daily heat unit accumulation and aggregates it over time. The accumulated heat units are normalized by the crop’s potential heat unit requirement to obtain a dimensionless development index. This index represents the progression from planting to physiological maturity. The resulting development stage serves as a coordinating variable for multiple downstream crop growth processes.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821266"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821268"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821269"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821272"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821274"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821275"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">deriving crop development stage from temperature data</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821278 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821278">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">heat-unit-based phenological development model</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This model simulates crop physiological development as a function of accumulated daily heat units. Development progresses from planting to physiological maturity based on temperatures exceeding a crop-specific base temperature. The accumulated heat units are normalized to a heat unit index that ranges from zero at planting to one at maturity. This index controls the timing of key developmental processes such as leaf area expansion, biomass partitioning, and harvest readiness. The approach provides a generic yet crop-specific representation of phenology using thermal time.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270"/>
        <mathmoddb:P147 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821277"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821274"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821275"/>
        <mathmoddb:P286 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821276"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">crop development driven by accumulated thermal time</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821279 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821279">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534292"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">crop phenological development</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">The research problem concerns predicting the progression of crop physiological development as influenced by temperature over time. Crop growth stages such as emergence, flowering, and maturity depend strongly on accumulated thermal energy rather than calendar time. The challenge is to represent this dependency in a general, crop-independent yet parameterizable way that can be applied across environments and management scenarios. The modeled solution translates daily temperature data into a normalized development index that governs downstream growth processes. This enables consistent coupling of phenology with biomass production, stress responses, and yield formation.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534269"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1513 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821278"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">predicting crop development timing from thermal conditions</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821280 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821280">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q60231"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ecophysiology</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P12 xml:lang="en">Q295425</mathmoddb:P12>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Ecophysiology is a scientific discipline that investigates how the physiological processes of organisms respond and adapt to environmental conditions. It focuses on interactions between biological function and external drivers such as temperature, light, water availability, and nutrient supply. The field seeks to explain how these interactions influence growth, development, reproduction, and survival across different environments. Ecophysiology bridges organismal physiology and ecology by linking internal mechanisms to environmental variability. It provides a mechanistic understanding of how organisms function under natural and managed conditions.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534268"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821279"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821316"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821356"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821359"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821365"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821392"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821394"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821395"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1560 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821433"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">study of adaptation of a organism&apos;s physiology to environmental conditions</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821281 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821281">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">intercepted photosynthetically active radiation</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Intercepted photosynthetically active radiation represents the portion of incoming solar radiation that is absorbed by the crop canopy and available for photosynthesis. It is computed as a function of total solar radiation and canopy leaf area. This quantity determines the energy input for potential biomass growth. It is a central driver of radiation-based crop growth models.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">radiation intercepted by the crop canopy</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821282 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821282">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">canopy light attenuation coefficient</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This coefficient quantifies the exponential attenuation of incoming radiation as it passes through a plant canopy. It represents the combined effects of absorption and scattering by leaves and other plant organs. The parameter is used in Beer–Lambert type equations to estimate radiation interception from leaf area index. Its value depends on canopy architecture and leaf orientation. It is a specialization of a general attenuation coefficient applied to plant canopies.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">attenuation of light within a plant canopy</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821283 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821283">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">photosynthetically active solar radiation fraction</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">solar radiation conversion fraction</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821284 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821284">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">potential biomass increment</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This quantity represents the increase in crop dry matter biomass during a single day under optimal conditions. It is computed from intercepted photosynthetically active radiation and a crop-specific conversion efficiency. The value reflects the maximum attainable biomass growth for that day. It contributes to the accumulation of total potential crop biomass over the growing season.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">potential daily increase in crop biomass</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821285 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821285">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">radiation use efficiency parameter</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This crop-specific parameter defines the efficiency with which intercepted photosynthetically active radiation is converted into dry matter biomass. It represents physiological and biochemical characteristics of the crop. Higher values indicate more efficient biomass production per unit of absorbed radiation. The parameter is assumed constant under optimal growth conditions.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">converts radiation into biomass</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821286 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821286">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">change in daylength</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This quantity represents the daily change in daylength relative to the previous day. It accounts for seasonal variation in photoperiod. It modifies the radiation-driven biomass production term. The quantity introduces a temporal adjustment to potential growth.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">daily change in daylight duration</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821287 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821287">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">daylength</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Daylength represents the number of hours between sunrise and sunset for a given day and location. It depends on Earth’s axial tilt and orbital position relative to the Sun.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">daylight duration</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821288 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821288">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">solar declination angle</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">The solar declination angle describes the angular position of the Sun relative to Earth’s equatorial plane. It varies predictably throughout the year due to Earth’s axial tilt. This angle determines the apparent height of the Sun and the length of daylight at a given latitude. It is a standard astronomical variable used in photoperiod calculations.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">angle between Sun and equatorial plane</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821289 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821289">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">day index</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">integer number identifying a specific day</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821290 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821290">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">daily change in leaf area index</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This quantity represents the daily change in leaf area index before the onset of leaf decline. The quantity controls the dynamic evolution of canopy size over time.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">increment in leaf area index</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821291 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821291">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">maximum leaf area index</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">maximum value of leaf area index for a specific crop</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821292 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821292">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">daily change in heat unit factor</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">factor driving leaf area index development</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821293 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821293">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">crop growth constraint</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">minimum stress factor - water, nutrients, aeration, temperature</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821294 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821294">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">leaf area index at start of decline</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">value of leaf area index at start of decline</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821295 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821295">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">heat unit index at start of leaf area index decline</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">heat unit index for specific point in growing season</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821296 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821296">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">leaf area index decline rate parameter</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">parameter that governs leaf area index decline for specific crop</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821297 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821297">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">heat unit factor</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">The heat unit factor expresses the relative progress of crop development on a normalized scale from zero to one. It is derived from the accumulated heat unit index using a crop-specific sigmoid function. HUF is used to regulate phenology-dependent growth processes. It provides a smooth, continuous representation of crop development stage.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">normalized crop development factor</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821298 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821298">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">heat unit response shape parameters</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">These crop-specific parameters determine the shape and steepness of the sigmoid relationship between heat unit index and heat unit factor. They are computed by fitting the heat unit factor equation to two predefined calibration points. The parameters remain constant throughout the simulation. They reflect phenological characteristics specific to each crop.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">shape parameters of HUF sigmoid curve</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821299 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821299">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">accumulated potential biomass</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This quantity represents the cumulative dry matter biomass produced by a crop under potential growth conditions. It is obtained by summing daily potential biomass increments over time. The value reflects the maximum attainable biomass prior to stress reduction and partitioning. It serves as the basis for modeling structural development and yield formation.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">total potential crop dry matter</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>



    <!-- https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821301 -->


    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821301">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
