        <mathmoddb:P989 xml:lang="en">&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; class=&quot;mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle=&quot;true&quot; scriptlevel=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;H&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;U&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;F&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;H&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mfrac&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;H&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;U&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;I&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;H&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;U&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;I&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;+&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mi&gt;e&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mn&gt;6.50&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;−&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;10.0&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;mi&gt;H&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;U&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;I&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mfrac&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P989>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">harvest index heat unit factor equation</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This equation computes a heat unit factor that controls the rate of harvest index development. The factor increases non-linearly with phenological development represented by the heat unit index. Parameter values are chosen so that most crop yield is produced during the second half of the growing season. The formulation reflects observed reproductive development patterns in grain crops.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">computes phenological scaling factor for harvest index</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
