        <mathmoddb:P983 xml:lang="en">&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; class=&quot;mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle=&quot;true&quot; scriptlevel=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;E&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;o&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
        <mathmoddb:P989 xml:lang="en">&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; class=&quot;mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle=&quot;true&quot; scriptlevel=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;E&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;P&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;E&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;o&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mfrac&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;L&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;A&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;I&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mn&gt;3&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mfrac&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P989>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">potential plant evaporation rate equation</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This equation estimates the potential plant evaporation rate as a fraction of the potential evaporation. The fraction depends on canopy development, represented by the leaf area index. The formulation constrains the potential plant evaporation rate so that it does not exceed the potential evaporation. It provides a simple representation of canopy resistance in the plant water use model.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <mathmoddb:P286 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821595"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">estimates potential plant evaporation rate from canopy size and potential evaporation</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
