        <mathmoddb:P989 xml:lang="en">&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; class=&quot;mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle=&quot;true&quot; scriptlevel=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;U&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;S&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;munderover&gt;&lt;mo movablelimits=&quot;false&quot; stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;∑&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;l&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;1&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;M&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/munderover&gt;&lt;mi&gt;U&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass=&quot;ORD&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;l&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P989>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">total soil nitrogen supply equation</rdfs:label>
        <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This equation computes the total nitrogen supply available to the crop by summing the layer-specific nitrogen supply rates. It represents the total nitrogen that could be taken up by mass flow on a given day. The result serves as an intermediate quantity used to compare soil nitrogen availability with crop nitrogen demand. It links soil-layer processes to whole-plant nitrogen uptake.</mathmoddb:P1459>
        <mathmoddb:P1460 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696"/>
        <mathmoddb:P1495 rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265"/>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">aggregates nitrogen supply from all soil layers</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
